{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7697","id":5211669435,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNqPDuw","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7697","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7697.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7697.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7697","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7697/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7697/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7697/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/statuses/7f31fadac97f4daa2c0bd5ba8e36857e39be21f7","number":7697,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(queue): standing issue↔queue coverage reconciliation (#7016)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #7016\n\n## Problem\n\nNothing reconciles the open-issue set against fleet-queue coverage. Issues enter the queue only when a creator-class lane files them (file + enqueue in the same pass); anything filed another way — a work lane filing a blocker mid-task, an audit lane, by hand, or predating the queue (epics) — silently never gets a queue item, so no lane ever dispositions it. The 2026-11-07 reconciliation found 23 such issues across the four repos; that day's import was a one-off.\n\n## What this adds\n\n**Broker — read-only `POST /coverage`.** Given the open-issue set the caller just enumerated, it answers per issue whether a **live** task (`queued`/`claimed`/`parked`/`blocked`) holds its repo-health dedupe key in the named queue. Per Drew's doctrine (2026-11-07): a `done` task is **not** coverage (done means triage or a landed slice, not a resolved issue), and neither is a task in a `*-shadow` queue. It never writes tasks or events.\n\n**`scripts/fleet/queue-reconcile/`** — the scheduled job:\n- enumerates open issues with `gh api --paginate` (PRs filtered out; a partial page would read as coverage that does not exist),\n- asks the broker for the diff,\n- with `--import`, enqueues a triage packet per uncovered issue **through the sanctioned CLI path**, dedupe-keyed `repo-health:v1:triage:<repo>:issue:<n>` so re-runs are idempotent by construction,\n- **observe-only by default**, matching the sweeper revalidator's two-step rollout,\n- a fetch or broker failure exits **3** and names the repo in an ERRORS section — it never reports as \"0 uncovered\".\n\n**systemd units** (hourly at :41, `Persistent`) + a row in `doc/fleet-schedule-registry.md` per the same-pass rule.\n\n**`AGENTS.md`**: the file-and-enqueue rule for issues filed outside a creator run.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [x] A scheduled reconciliation exists — `queue-coverage-reconcile.timer`, hourly, persistent.\n- [ ] Its first run reports 0 uncovered — **pending deployment**: the units are repo-shipped but not installed, and the running broker does not yet serve `/coverage` (it needs a rebuild + restart). Verified end-to-end today: GitHub enumeration succeeds, the broker answers `unknown command /coverage`, and the script exits 3 with the repo named rather than reporting a false zero. Once the broker is redeployed the timer's first cycle produces the real number in `~/.local/state/queue-reconcile/latest.md`.\n- [x] The file-and-enqueue rule is written into `AGENTS.md`.\n\n## Unrelated fix included\n\n`validate.rs`: `FLEET_REPOS` is declared `[&str; 10]` but holds **9** entries, so the `fleet-queue` lib test target does not compile at `main` with `--all-features`. CI does not build this crate, so the defect was invisible there. One-character fix; it blocks the test target this change needs.\n\n## Tests\n\n```\ncargo test -p fleet-queue --all-features\n  100 passed (lib), 2 passed (integration), 0 failed\npython3 -I scripts/fleet/queue-reconcile/test_check_coverage.py\n  6 passed\n```\n\nNew coverage: 4 parser cases + 2 `proptest` properties on the dedupe-key parser (canonical keys round-trip for every class and dispatch suffix; another repo's key never matches), and 6 offline script tests (observe imports nothing, import enqueues exactly the uncovered set, full coverage imports nothing, fetch failure is an error not a zero, packet shape, report written).\n\nThe packet the script builds validates against the live broker: `repo-queue validate` → `packet valid (repo-task/v1)`.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796736176&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7697&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7697&signature=553b385515abbfff4257c50e6f968e65058a9b25ff3c046699ac4d73e40b8897\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7697?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T13:22:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T05:43:03Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T05:43:00Z","merged_at":"2026-11-09T05:43:00Z","merge_commit_sha":"e74e657140fa96afab7dfc1896e8d564efdff712","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[{"id":7767549,"node_id":"T_kwDOAZNvF84AdoX9","url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549","members_url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549/members{/member}","name":"codeowners","description":"Team Discussions: developing-today/code","permission":"pull","privacy":"closed","notification_setting":"notifications_enabled","html_url":"https://github.com/orgs/developing-today/teams/codeowners","repositories_url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549/repos","slug":"codeowners","type":"organization","organization_id":26439447,"parent":null}],"head":{"label":"developing-today:queue/11447-7016-queue-coverage-reconciliation","ref":"queue/11447-7016-queue-coverage-reconciliation","repo":{"id":627308783,"node_id":"R_kgDOJWP47w","name":"code","full_name":"developing-today/code","owner":{"login":"developing-today","id":26439447,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI2NDM5NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/develo